{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, remove inventory temporary files in /var/tmp/inventory after they reach seven days of age while retaining newer files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service uses a seven-day modification-age threshold scoped to /var/tmp/inventory. Direct testing showed the prepared expired file was removed, the current file remained unchanged, and cleanup completed successfully before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-308898cb51fa4708","cmd-dec6417045904bf9","cmd-0efb8ac44413414d","cmd-a565c43fc09643da"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Run the inventory cleanup automatically every day.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd timer was enabled and active, linked to the cleanup service, configured with OnCalendar=daily and Persistent=true, and scheduled for the next midnight. This state persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f695581670494a06","cmd-0efb8ac44413414d","cmd-a565c43fc09643da"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so none remained or required reversion. Creating the two intended units, reloading/enabling the timer, bounded cleanup invocations, and the mandated restart all had clear task or evidence-protocol roles. The failed SSH service predated execution and remained unchanged; package health remained intact. Observed temporary-file and socket changes were normal restart effects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-41fd77734a974f29","cmd-e5c77a614f29411c","cmd-f695581670494a06","cmd-dec6417045904bf9","cmd-c88a4c0ea54e491b","cmd-3375f1ce9fa14b01","cmd-bb569db8bbc04dd1","cmd-a565c43fc09643da","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both public task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory restart protocol also showed a pre-restart boot identity and task health, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered timer, service, and retained data. The boot transition is independently corroborated by the fixed after-prepare and after-executor observations.","limitations":["The evidence window did not span the next scheduled midnight, so a naturally elapsed daily firing was not observed; automation is supported by the live enabled/active timer, its next-elapse time, and its daily configuration.","Whole-node systemd state was degraded before and after execution because ssh.service was already failed. Consequently, restart evidence establishes recovery of the task service and data but not an entirely healthy whole-node baseline; the fixed failed-service snapshots show this was pre-existing and not executor-caused."]}
